p Last updated October 28, 2026.

p
  | This policy describes
  strong  SF Parking
  |, an iOS app made by Cezary Wojcik. The app looks up San Francisco street parking rules and can save where you parked.

h2 Location

p
  | The app uses your location only while you are using it. The map shows where you are, and asking for the rules at your current spot takes a single location reading. The app does not track your location in the background.

p
  | You can also tap a street, or run a Shortcut that passes in a location. The coordinate of the spot you look up is sent to the City and County of San Francisco's open data service,
  a(href="https://data.sfgov.org")  DataSF
  |, to fetch street sweeping schedules, parking regulations, and meter locations for that block. I do not receive a copy of that request, and I do not run the service that answers it.

h2 What stays on your phone

p
  | Saved spots, parking history, your residential permit area, and reminder settings stay on your device. Widgets and the Live Activity on that device read the same on-device data. Nothing in that history is uploaded to a server I operate.

p
  | There is no account. You can remove a saved spot or clear history in the app. Deleting the app removes the rest.

h2 Notifications

p Move-by reminders are scheduled on your phone. They are not sent through a server I run.

h2 Maps

p
  | Maps are provided by Apple. When the map is on screen, Apple receives the usual request for that area.
  a(href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/")  Apple's privacy policy
  |  describes how Apple handles that.

h2 What the app does not do

ul
  li It does not sell your data.
  li It does not show ads.
  li It does not include analytics or tracking.
  li It does not ask you to create an account.

h2 This website

p
  | cezarywojcik.com is a separate personal site. The contact form emails me what you submit (including your IP address) so I can reply, and blog posts may load comments from Disqus. The SF Parking app does not include any of that.

h2 Contact

p
  | Questions about this policy or the app go through the
  a(href="/contact")  contact form
  |.

h2 Changes

p If the app's data practices change, I will update this page. The date at the top is the latest revision.
